abstract: >-
  Python implementation of the algorithms and of the numerical experiments of
  the article. The code solves the Cauchy problem u'(t) + (A + B(t)) u(t) =
  f(t) in a Hilbert space, where A is self-adjoint positive definite and B(t)
  is a bounded time-dependent operator. It contains the perturbation
  algorithm, which reduces the purely implicit four-layer scheme (three-step
  backward differentiation formula, BDF3) to three two-layer schemes; the
  four-layer scheme itself; and the iterative realization in which only the
  time-independent operator I + tau A is inverted. The script
  run_experiments.py reproduces the data of all tables and figures of
  Section 7 of the article. Requirements: Python >= 3.8 and NumPy >= 1.20.
